      "verbatim_texts": [
        "For MyCorp, the process begins by entering expenses."
      ],
      "justification": "Implicitly initiates the process and directly describes the contextual start and first action."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n3"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "After entering expenses, the next step is to generate a spreadsheet."
      ],
      "justification": "Direct paraphrase of the spreadsheet generation step."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n4"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Once the spreadsheet is generated, the request can be approved or disapproved."
      ],
      "justification": "Captures the condition evaluation and the resulting exclusive choice split."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b1->n5",
        "action:n5"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "However, if the request is approved, the expenses can be paid out."
      ],
      "justification": "Guard models the approved condition; action models the payout."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b1->c1"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the request is not approved, the process goes back to entering expenses."
      ],
      "justification": "Guard captures the negative outcome condition leading to the convergence point."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n7"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "The process then checks again if the request is approved or not."
      ],
      "justification": "Models the second approval check and its corresponding decision gateway."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b2->n8",
        "action:n8"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "But if it is approved, the expenses can be paid out."
      ],
      "justification": "Guard captures the approved condition; action models the second payout instance."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b2->c1"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If it is not approved, the process goes back to entering expenses."
      ],
      "justification": "Guard captures the second negative outcome condition merging into the convergence point."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "converge:c1"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the request is not approved, the process goes back to entering expenses.",
        "If it is not approved, the process goes back to entering expenses."
      ],
      "justification": "Structural node representing the rejoining of both rejection paths before looping back."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n10"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Finally, after the expenses are paid out, the process comes to an end."
      ],
      "justification": "Explicit closing statement maps to the final action and terminal node."
